 {R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0,$ the invertible matrix theorem implies that $T$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $T$ is not invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-141569/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "113a601e-220a-54a3-a64b-1e554bc3d79f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141569"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140085/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "0afb9c94-12b9-546a-b4a5-4ad634e9315a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140085/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "27232887-ff74-5d38-b262-c8d644c09615" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140085/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "4c14eb22-8c7f-507d-a725-41bbb1d74c97" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140085/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "627d755b-0e11-5012-8dda-dd5cb7612092" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140085/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "49c26b2c-ebf0-5259-a65b-534a5e9eddbb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140085/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "375775ac-a6ec-5f30-9961-c00792c0e83f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct 